{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792698397,"nonce":"tCVpOq3KIDGSuOxfU05E5T+7IPo=","message":"Investigated and fixed the retained image atlas and reduced mounted-editor overhead. Ashui commits a5149651c00e0e45e1602a55538d8289e29df54e and 353516cef69c2bc7c8bdb723e99e17e8a438dfb7 are committed locally, with RayDE pinned to the latter. No pushes or Rayzor edits/builds.\n\nAtlas cause and fix: Bitmap.dispose and RayDE's manual SVG intern-table removal did not invalidate the renderer's cached images. Added disposal revisions, idempotent SvgDocument.dispose, and renderer repacking on resource disposal; RayDE now uses the public API after the last owned SVG use. Shelf packing also required an unnecessary trailing pixel outside a texture's edge: a 2048-square image forced a 4096-square (64 MiB) atlas. It now fits a 2048-square (16 MiB) atlas. Internal neighbour spacing remains. freePixels/gpuOnly semantics were preserved.\n\nEditor cause and fix: the active editor mounted styled text widgets for whitespace and syntax tokens far outside the horizontal viewport. Ashui now omits whitespace runs without explicit token styles and culls horizontal runs with bucketed overscan, retaining full source geometry and syntax caches. Small horizontal pans reuse the same widget identities. CodeMetrics.xAt now binary-searches the same ordered caret stops instead of scanning them for every token boundary.\n\nIsolated native editor on tests/ExplorerMemoryProbe.hx, same 960x650 editor inside a 1280x800 window:\n- Full editor before: 153.4 MiB physical, 41.1 MiB occupied GC blocks, 1232 nodes, 996 token/probe nodes.\n- Without minimap: 131.6 MiB physical; plain highlighting: 114.1 MiB.\n- Whitespace-only change: 146.9 MiB, 957 nodes, 721 token/probe nodes.\n- Both token changes: 117.1 MiB physical, 25.8 MiB blocks, 584 nodes, 348 token/probe nodes.\nThe highlighter/document data and minimap remain enabled in the final comparison. Artifacts: bin/editor-memory-before-results/, editor-memory-trimmed-results/, editor-memory-windowed-results/.\n\nFull native mixed-workspace run, 16 Markdown previews, 32 real large Haxe files, Git sidebar and graph, eight raster images and eight SVGs. All 65 tabs opened and closed in opening order; the probe additionally returned to code with all tabs still open. Physical footprint MiB:\n- Baseline 144.3.\n- Initial Haxe phase collected: 512.3 (previous cache-packing run 506.4; this initial phase did NOT improve).\n- All 65 tabs, SVG active, collected: 379.6 (previous 440.0).\n- All 65 tabs, code active, collected: 382.3; image atlas falls to 256 KiB.\n- Last SVG restored: 389.1; its active image uses a 16 MiB atlas.\n- All tabs closed, 30s idle, collected: 317.1.\n- LSP stopped and collected: 304.5 (previous 363.3); remaining UI images use a 1 MiB atlas instead of 64 MiB.\n- Process peak 569.8 MiB (previous 675.1).\n\nEditor, document, buffer, editorRef, syntax, image, canvas and owned preview-SVG counts all return to zero. Workspace build.hxml and .rayde/recent.txt retain their original hashes. Final marked-line storage is 16.5 MiB inside 73.4 MiB occupied GC blocks. The process still retains native/allocator capacity above its initial floor, so the original issue remains open.\n\nLSP qualification: the same bin/rayzor SHA256 7809c5ec0df16e2e4a59a2a556b438ecffb4e61231af124c72435ab81178b91d ran separately. At the Haxe/code checkpoints 31/32 documents had published analysis completion, but only one of 32 explicit symbol requests returned a non-null answer. There were 1069 workspace diagnostics. Server footprint grew to about 1.3 GiB, including after didClose; this is separate from RayDE and remains for the server session. The run also recorded long GC pauses, including an explicit collection at t=331.86s with 4179.65ms stop/prep, 5765.33ms mark and 914.95ms sweep (10859.93ms total). Other local verification was running during the experiment; no UI-latency improvement is claimed, and initial loading/GC pressure remains unresolved.\n\nValidation: Ashui ImageResidencyPixels passes opt-in/shared residency plus bitmap/SVG disposal, idempotence, reparsing, atlas resizing and remaining-image checks. EditorTokenPixels passes complete-row pixel comparisons (one-channel clip-edge AA tolerance), Unicode/tab caret parity, horizontal/vertical pans and small-pan widget reuse in both schemes. EditorLayersPixels and CodeFindTest pass. RayDE document lifecycle and image/SVG snapshot scenarios pass in both schemes. Full native probe exits zero, Main AOT lowers all functions with zero refusals, native smoke succeeds using isolated HOME, and app signature verification passes. Native launcher and AOT bundle rebuilt; previous executable is bin/rayde-before-atlas-optimization.\n\nArtifacts: bin/mixed-workspace-optimized-results/results.json, summary.json, context.json, raw vmmap files and heap censuses. Source probes now record the atlas separately, token counts, diagnostics, and all-tabs code/image switching. The matching pinned CSS compiler and unchanged native build were reused locally rather than creating another Cargo target.","files":null}]}